1
00:00:23,223 --> 00:00:25,158
Oh, are you the owner of Club Carte?

2
00:00:25,792 --> 00:00:26,793
No, I'm not.

3
00:00:27,594 --> 00:00:29,863
I didn't expect to see you here.

4
00:00:31,765 --> 00:00:34,934
I heard your manger snatched
the money and ran.

5
00:00:35,268 --> 00:00:36,469
It's not me.

6
00:00:37,637 --> 00:00:39,906
Are you sure it's not you?

7
00:00:40,373 --> 00:00:41,341
I'm sure.

8
00:00:42,675 --> 00:00:43,510
Wait.

9
00:00:45,045 --> 00:00:48,448
<i>This is a story about</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

10
00:00:49,282 --> 00:00:51,885
<i>University hospitals</i>
<i>lost their authorities.</i>

11
00:00:51,951 --> 00:00:53,887
<i>It's entered into the law of jungle.</i>

12
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:57,991
<i>To save this crisis</i>
<i>in the world of medical care,</i>

13
00:00:58,625 --> 00:01:02,929
<i>a freelance doctor, in other words,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor appeared.</i>

14
00:01:03,596 --> 00:01:06,933
<i>Executive manager</i>
<i>of the surgery department,</i>

15
00:01:08,268 --> 00:01:14,941
<i>Dr. Hiruma makes his rounds</i>
<i>for the second surgery.</i>

16
00:01:17,177 --> 00:01:19,913
Why is Kondo walking ahead of us?

17
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:23,349
Prof. Hiruma must love his thesis.

18
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:26,586
Kidney and small bowel
exchange transplant?

19
00:01:26,786 --> 00:01:29,556
Kondo, do you have plans tonight?

20
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:31,224
No.

21
00:01:32,692 --> 00:01:35,095
My wife would like to invite you over.

22
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:37,831
She'll cook something for you.

23
00:01:38,398 --> 00:01:39,399
I'd love to.

24
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:44,170
Probably she'll order
catered food though.

25
00:01:46,239 --> 00:01:48,575
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

26
00:01:49,509 --> 00:01:53,246
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

27
00:01:54,013 --> 00:01:59,119
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

28
00:01:59,586 --> 00:02:01,054
Good morning, Daimon.

29
00:02:02,255 --> 00:02:03,089
Greet him.

30
00:02:03,456 --> 00:02:05,358
You're scary as usual.

31
00:02:05,525 --> 00:02:07,260
- What do you mean?
- Your face is scary.

32
00:02:09,762 --> 00:02:10,763
Is that your greeting?

33
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:18,638
You have a guest.

34
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:21,241
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon...</i>

35
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:22,142
My guest?

36
00:02:22,242 --> 00:02:25,145
<i>...also known as Doctor-X.</i>

37
00:02:38,191 --> 00:02:40,226
Daimon, do I have a guest?

38
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:43,129
Hiruma.

39
00:02:45,265 --> 00:02:46,132
Hiruma?

40
00:02:51,137 --> 00:02:53,006
Finally I found you.

41
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:57,343
Long time no see, Dr. Hiruma.

42
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:03,716
Please come in. We have a guest.

43
00:03:06,619 --> 00:03:08,154
Please sit down...Oh?

44
00:03:09,489 --> 00:03:11,958
How long have you been his lover?

45
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:14,260
I'm his secretary.

46
00:03:15,094 --> 00:03:17,430
Does he still wear
those polka-dot boxers?

47
00:03:18,798 --> 00:03:21,768
Recently, he wears
Louis Vuitton's polka-dot boxers.

48
00:03:22,168 --> 00:03:23,002
Any comments?

49
00:03:23,636 --> 00:03:27,407
It doesn't matter,
polka-dot or Louis Vuitton.

50
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:29,642
I'm wearing plaid boxers today.

51
00:03:32,312 --> 00:03:33,146
Have a seat.

52
00:03:37,917 --> 00:03:41,554
Congratulations on being promoted
to executive manager.

53
00:03:42,789 --> 00:03:44,357
I've finally said that to you.

54
00:03:45,992 --> 00:03:47,160
You're so sarcastic.

55
00:03:47,694 --> 00:03:53,800
I've really tried to visit your place.

56
00:03:53,866 --> 00:03:58,671
Since I became
the executive manager, though,

57
00:03:58,771 --> 00:04:01,808
I've been so busy. It's been so hard
to have my own time...

58
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:06,112
I still remember
the election five years ago.

59
00:04:06,346 --> 00:04:07,180
I know. Yep.

60
00:04:09,115 --> 00:04:10,650
Thanks to you,

61
00:04:11,618 --> 00:04:13,786
I've gotten this position.

62
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,522
I do appreciate you.

63
00:04:17,357 --> 00:04:21,594
Then could you do me a favor?

64
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:25,565
Dr. Daimon, who's that woman?

65
00:04:25,632 --> 00:04:26,466
I don't know.

66
00:04:26,599 --> 00:04:28,568
- Are you a real doctor?
- Yeah?

67
00:04:29,035 --> 00:04:31,037
- Wanna keep your position?
- Yeah.

68
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:35,541
You must know that woman
if you're a doctor.

69
00:04:35,842 --> 00:04:36,843
Is she a big shot?

70
00:04:37,143 --> 00:04:38,444
Rumiko Shijo,

71
00:04:38,511 --> 00:04:40,380
the owner of Club Nakazono in Ginza.

72
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:43,583
She has connections
with business, politics,

73
00:04:43,716 --> 00:04:45,118
and medical industries.

74
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:46,519
A queen of Ginza.

75
00:04:46,586 --> 00:04:48,187
Very influential.

76
00:04:48,688 --> 00:04:50,256
Some say that Hiruma won the election

77
00:04:50,757 --> 00:04:54,627
for the executive manager
five years ago because of her power.

78
00:04:54,694 --> 00:04:58,831
She's considered as
the behind-the-scene key player.

79
00:04:58,898 --> 00:05:02,035
She is called "Secret Nakazono."

80
00:05:02,101 --> 00:05:04,570
She knows many secrets of big shots.

81
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:05,972
Secret Nakazono?

82
00:05:06,339 --> 00:05:09,509
She used to be Hiruma's lover.

83
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:14,981
She'll do something for the
next election of new chairperson?

84
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:18,618
Probably. If Hiruma's
favorite professor won,

85
00:05:18,885 --> 00:05:20,653
Hiruma's system will be complete.

86
00:05:21,087 --> 00:05:23,589
Will bundles of cash be used?

87
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:25,525
That's the election.

88
00:05:25,725 --> 00:05:27,026
Stop your aimless chats.

89
00:05:29,062 --> 00:05:30,897
Tsuruta, you have surgery.

90
00:05:31,531 --> 00:05:32,365
Sorry.

91
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:36,536
I'll do that for you. I'm so bored.

92
00:05:37,370 --> 00:05:39,939
And you can continue
talking about the cash.

93
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,741
No thanks.

94
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:43,343
Whatever.

95
00:05:47,447 --> 00:05:48,381
Prof. Ebina.

96
00:05:49,382 --> 00:05:50,983
I apologize that I walked next to

97
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:55,088
Executive Manager Hiruma,
even though I'm still an instructor.

98
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,227
It's all right.

99
00:06:01,661 --> 00:06:03,463
Don't worry, Kondo.

100
00:06:05,264 --> 00:06:06,733
Executive Manager calls for you.

101
00:06:06,933 --> 00:06:07,900
What?

102
00:06:15,074 --> 00:06:19,579
We found stage 4 tumor cells
on the distal pancreas.

103
00:06:21,314 --> 00:06:24,884
The tumor cells are invading the
surrounding vessels and nerves.

104
00:06:27,754 --> 00:06:29,155
Is it cancer?

105
00:06:30,690 --> 00:06:33,926
Yeah. I'm very sorry,
but you have cancer.

106
00:06:34,827 --> 00:06:39,499
Since the aneurism is
on the adjacent abdominal aorta,

107
00:06:40,299 --> 00:06:44,003
it's difficult to
remove the tumor by surgery.

108
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:49,475
I'm going to die...

109
00:06:49,876 --> 00:06:50,843
Wait a minute.

110
00:06:51,210 --> 00:06:53,846
Nobody says
that you're going to die.

111
00:06:54,647 --> 00:06:57,049
Let's use the GS treatment.

112
00:06:57,116 --> 00:07:01,254
It's a kind of chemo therapy
to eliminate your tumor.

113
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:04,857
Regarding the aneurism
on the abdominal aorta,

114
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:08,694
we'll wait and see
while preventing it from being ruptured.

115
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:10,663
I think that's the best treatment.

116
00:07:11,464 --> 00:07:12,398
Operate on me.

117
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:16,803
Hiruma, you can do it.

118
00:07:17,804 --> 00:07:19,772
Well, um...

119
00:07:20,006 --> 00:07:23,843
I can, but it's impossible.

120
00:07:24,210 --> 00:07:25,445
It would be unreasonable.

121
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:29,682
This operation will
come with a huge risk.

122
00:07:29,916 --> 00:07:32,752
- Just in case...
- I don't care.

123
00:07:39,358 --> 00:07:41,327
- You know this.
- Of course.

124
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:45,164
I'll disclose all your secrets
in this note pad to the public.

125
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:50,770
It reveals how you've obtained
the current position.

126
00:07:58,611 --> 00:08:00,847
- Stop joking...
- I'm serious.

127
00:08:03,649 --> 00:08:04,717
If I die,

128
00:08:07,086 --> 00:08:08,955
your career as a doctor will be over.

129
00:08:15,094 --> 00:08:16,062
I don't want that.

130
00:08:19,599 --> 00:08:21,467
You know Club Nakazono's owner, too?

131
00:08:22,401 --> 00:08:25,071
I met her
at my mentor's 60th birthday party.

132
00:08:25,605 --> 00:08:28,140
No good. Should I greet her?

133
00:08:28,207 --> 00:08:30,810
A medical intern should wait
for another 10 years.

134
00:08:33,546 --> 00:08:35,948
- Thanks for your hard work.
- Rumiko.

135
00:08:36,916 --> 00:08:40,152
Hi, Kameyama.
I haven't seen you recently.

136
00:08:40,219 --> 00:08:42,555
- Miho misses you.
- She does?

137
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:45,024
- Visit her sometimes.
- I'd love to.

138
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:46,726
Excuse me.

139
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:50,229
Oh? Are you a newbie?

140
00:08:51,163 --> 00:08:53,299
Here, this is my business card.

141
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,402
Thank you very much!

142
00:08:56,502 --> 00:08:59,105
It must have been said
you should wait for 10 years.

143
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:01,173
Please come by, though.

144
00:09:01,274 --> 00:09:02,708
Okay. I'll be there tonight.

145
00:09:02,942 --> 00:09:04,310
Let me take this operation.

146
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:05,444
Oh?

147
00:09:05,578 --> 00:09:06,879
Are you a doctor?

148
00:09:07,413 --> 00:09:09,649
- What's your position?
- I'm a freelance surgeon.

149
00:09:09,782 --> 00:09:11,617
- A part-timer?
- A freelancer.

150
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:13,719
Wanna come work for me?

151
00:09:13,886 --> 00:09:15,054
A full-time position.

152
00:09:15,354 --> 00:09:17,456
You'll earn more than
being a doctor.

153
00:09:19,492 --> 00:09:20,459
No thanks.

154
00:09:24,297 --> 00:09:26,766
You can't have her.

155
00:09:27,533 --> 00:09:30,102
She'd cut even a bruise
with a knife.

156
00:09:31,904 --> 00:09:33,506
She seems interesting.

157
00:09:35,274 --> 00:09:37,376
So a hostess can earn that much?

158
00:09:37,443 --> 00:09:39,545
Never been to a bar like that?

159
00:09:40,046 --> 00:09:42,615
She has been to a night club.

160
00:09:43,115 --> 00:09:46,886
You can be a good hostess.

161
00:09:46,953 --> 00:09:52,258
Who wants to drink with
such an unfriendly hostess like her?

162
00:09:52,325 --> 00:09:53,326
Ron!

163
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:58,331
Concealed self-draw,
peace and manakan.

164
00:09:58,397 --> 00:10:00,032
I kick butt!

165
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:02,635
- Your butt got kicked.
- Why?

166
00:10:02,702 --> 00:10:04,370
You can't win with your discarded tile.

167
00:10:05,504 --> 00:10:08,641
It's called "furiten,"
and you blew it.

168
00:10:09,542 --> 00:10:13,112
- Sorry.
- You're the last again.

169
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:16,882
This is Kanbara.
May I speak to the owner?

170
00:10:17,149 --> 00:10:20,152
To whom are you calling?
Let's play it again.

171
00:10:20,219 --> 00:10:21,420
Club Nakazono's owner.

172
00:10:21,487 --> 00:10:23,422
This is a sales call. Be quiet.

173
00:10:27,426 --> 00:10:29,428
Ma'am, this is for you.

174
00:10:29,495 --> 00:10:30,329
Thanks.

175
00:10:31,897 --> 00:10:32,732
Hello?

176
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:35,901
Long time no see, Akira.

177
00:10:36,102 --> 00:10:39,138
Will you involve yourself
in the next election?

178
00:10:39,872 --> 00:10:41,240
Did Hiruma ask you?

179
00:10:42,208 --> 00:10:43,843
That's like him.

180
00:10:44,443 --> 00:10:46,379
So he won't have to perform surgery on me.

181
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:48,014
Are you ill?

182
00:10:48,347 --> 00:10:53,252
Tell Hiruma that I have a plan
if he won't do what I've asked.

183
00:11:00,526 --> 00:11:01,827
Rumiko? What's wrong?

184
00:11:02,962 --> 00:11:04,196
Are you all right?

185
00:11:05,898 --> 00:11:08,401
Boss!

186
00:11:08,467 --> 00:11:11,137
Call the ambulance! Hurry!

187
00:11:13,606 --> 00:11:14,607
That's no good.

188
00:11:24,650 --> 00:11:25,484
Excuse me.

189
00:11:27,553 --> 00:11:30,790
It's impossible to
perform surgery on Rumiko.

190
00:11:34,427 --> 00:11:40,566
About the conference in Kyoto this week.

191
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:42,535
Yes?

192
00:11:43,769 --> 00:11:47,606
I was thinking which of you
should come with me,

193
00:11:48,774 --> 00:11:50,109
you or Kondo.

194
00:11:51,744 --> 00:11:52,645
Yes.

195
00:11:52,912 --> 00:11:55,414
Now I've made up my mind.

196
00:11:57,817 --> 00:11:59,785
I will take Kondo with me.

197
00:12:03,189 --> 00:12:06,358
Is that because
you've acknowledged his thesis?

198
00:12:06,492 --> 00:12:07,326
No.

199
00:12:08,327 --> 00:12:09,328
That's not true.

200
00:12:30,116 --> 00:12:30,950
Ebina,

201
00:12:32,318 --> 00:12:35,488
you hold on to my life.

202
00:12:36,989 --> 00:12:37,823
Your life?

203
00:12:40,659 --> 00:12:43,996
While I'm away, take care of Rumiko.

204
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:49,568
So, save my life.

205
00:12:54,406 --> 00:12:58,444
Either way,
she won't last too long.

206
00:13:01,981 --> 00:13:06,752
The problem is her note pad.

207
00:13:11,690 --> 00:13:16,395
This is more important than

208
00:13:17,396 --> 00:13:21,367
attending the conference.

209
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:27,306
I'm counting on you, Ebina.

210
00:13:37,283 --> 00:13:38,184
Yes, sir.

211
00:13:45,691 --> 00:13:46,525
Yes, sir.

212
00:13:50,362 --> 00:13:52,398
What should we do?

213
00:13:52,464 --> 00:13:53,299
Move.

214
00:13:54,133 --> 00:13:54,967
Who are you?

215
00:13:55,968 --> 00:13:56,802
Move.

216
00:13:57,937 --> 00:13:59,038
Are you alright?

217
00:14:07,713 --> 00:14:09,114
Michiko.

218
00:14:10,082 --> 00:14:11,317
Cardiopulmonary arrest.

219
00:14:11,650 --> 00:14:14,453
Bring something to
wrap her up and ice cubes.

220
00:14:15,721 --> 00:14:16,622
Hurry!

221
00:14:22,228 --> 00:14:23,062
Akira, go on.

222
00:14:27,766 --> 00:14:30,436
- How many minutes already?
- Not more than ten minutes.

223
00:14:30,569 --> 00:14:31,937
Otherwise, she can't make it.

224
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:35,341
- Bring alcohol.
- Yes!

225
00:14:39,511 --> 00:14:41,513
- Here.
- Higher one.

226
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:42,581
Higher?

227
00:14:43,282 --> 00:14:46,385
- How about this?
- Higher.

228
00:14:46,619 --> 00:14:48,921
The Hennessey is quite expensive.

229
00:14:49,054 --> 00:14:50,422
A higher alcohol percentage!

230
00:15:03,802 --> 00:15:06,438
The heat of evaporation?
Great idea.

231
00:15:07,606 --> 00:15:09,174
The ambulance has arrived.

232
00:15:09,675 --> 00:15:13,445
Prepare the AED.

233
00:15:35,401 --> 00:15:39,805
Continue therapeutic hypothermia.
Keep her temperature at 34C.

234
00:15:40,706 --> 00:15:42,274
Might be cardiac tamponade.

235
00:15:42,408 --> 00:15:44,543
Check it on the echo.

236
00:15:47,313 --> 00:15:49,581
Pericardial fluid is found.
Venula needle, 16G.

237
00:15:50,482 --> 00:15:51,383
I'll move the bed.

238
00:16:13,672 --> 00:16:14,873
Cardiorespiratory is back.

239
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:18,310
Draw blood and test anti-virus.

240
00:16:18,544 --> 00:16:20,346
- Yes, ma'am.
- Anti-virus.

241
00:16:24,950 --> 00:16:27,052
Daimon. How is she?

242
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:31,357
She won't have brain damage...

243
00:16:31,423 --> 00:16:32,257
Okay.

244
00:16:34,593 --> 00:16:35,427
Thanks.

245
00:16:36,028 --> 00:16:38,063
Her surgery needs to be done soon.

246
00:16:39,665 --> 00:16:40,566
Let me do it.

247
00:16:42,868 --> 00:16:46,005
Stay away from this patient.

248
00:16:46,071 --> 00:16:47,406
Something is going on?

249
00:16:49,475 --> 00:16:51,643
You're an outsider.

250
00:16:55,781 --> 00:16:57,416
Oh, this is from the chief.

251
00:16:58,317 --> 00:17:02,087
The overtime charge is 30,000 yen
per hour, and night shift is 20,000 yen.

252
00:17:02,154 --> 00:17:04,556
The Hennessey
and vodka cost 250,000 yen.

253
00:17:04,623 --> 00:17:05,858
Ice cubes cost 50,000 yen.

254
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:09,595
But the service charge is free.
That's what he said.

255
00:17:10,562 --> 00:17:11,530
What's that?

256
00:17:12,765 --> 00:17:13,899
Please take care of it.

257
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:15,667
What does that mean?

258
00:17:19,405 --> 00:17:20,339
Hennessey?

259
00:17:20,973 --> 00:17:22,207
She's already hospitalized?

260
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:28,714
Michiko Daimon shouldn't have done that.

261
00:17:29,148 --> 00:17:33,118
There's still a chance that
she may have brain disorder.

262
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:37,856
- If it happens...
- Yeah. That could be possible.

263
00:17:38,090 --> 00:17:41,493
I take the responsibility
for being in charge.

264
00:17:42,361 --> 00:17:44,363
- So, don't worry.
- Okay. Thanks.

265
00:17:45,364 --> 00:17:47,399
Ebina, I'm counting on you.

266
00:17:49,468 --> 00:17:50,302
Yes, sir.

267
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:59,611
Yuka, do you like Dr. Kondo?

268
00:18:04,650 --> 00:18:09,521
Kondo performs surgery perfectly,

269
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,790
and his thesis is splendid.

270
00:18:12,458 --> 00:18:14,827
As you see, he's very handsome.

271
00:18:15,461 --> 00:18:19,731
He has everything
a surgeon should have.

272
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:22,634
No, I don't. But thank you.

273
00:18:24,736 --> 00:18:28,640
You may need to clear
your personal connections though,

274
00:18:28,874 --> 00:18:30,209
especially with women.

275
00:18:30,742 --> 00:18:32,144
That's rude.

276
00:18:32,511 --> 00:18:35,013
Dr. Kondo is different from you.

277
00:18:35,214 --> 00:18:36,348
Is that so?

278
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:40,085
I'm a clumsy man.

279
00:18:41,987 --> 00:18:45,891
- What a nice excuse, handsome dude.
- Honey.

280
00:18:47,359 --> 00:18:50,129
Let's open a bottle of champagne.

281
00:18:50,329 --> 00:18:53,065
We have Dom Perignon, Gold.

282
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:58,437
Hold on. Not Gold. Rose is fine.

283
00:19:13,018 --> 00:19:14,052
Dr. Kondo.

284
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:17,156
Yes?

285
00:19:18,757 --> 00:19:24,163
If you want me, you've got to
achieve more than what my dad has.

286
00:19:39,611 --> 00:19:40,445
Are you up?

287
00:19:42,114 --> 00:19:43,015
Ebina?

288
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:45,150
You were in an urgent condition.

289
00:19:45,884 --> 00:19:49,054
Viral myocarditis caused
the cardiac inflammation.

290
00:19:49,221 --> 00:19:50,088
I see.

291
00:19:52,558 --> 00:19:54,960
I guess I still have some luck.

292
00:19:58,430 --> 00:20:02,401
Hiruma asked you to babysit me, didn't he?

293
00:20:03,602 --> 00:20:04,436
Babysit you?

294
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:07,239
He always puts his issues on others.

295
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:10,108
He's always been that way.

296
00:20:13,312 --> 00:20:14,313
Are you okay?

297
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:20,219
Perform surgery on me, Ebina.

298
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:22,688
If you succeed,

299
00:20:22,988 --> 00:20:24,389
I'll give you my note pad

300
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:27,025
that contains Hiruma's secrets.

301
00:20:27,092 --> 00:20:31,797
With my note pad,
you can bring him down.

302
00:20:32,297 --> 00:20:36,401
You don't have to
be Hiruma's brown-noser.

303
00:20:38,837 --> 00:20:40,138
Depending on how you use it,

304
00:20:40,806 --> 00:20:43,642
you'll be the executive manager
of the surgery department.

305
00:20:44,776 --> 00:20:47,179
The executive manager?

306
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:54,286
Every winner has gambled
at his crucial period.

307
00:20:55,587 --> 00:20:58,890
He won and succeeded in his life.

308
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:05,297
This is your time to take a risk.

309
00:21:11,570 --> 00:21:13,071
I can't perform surgery.

310
00:21:14,473 --> 00:21:20,412
Executive Manager Hiruma has
brought me up here.

311
00:21:21,413 --> 00:21:22,247
Excuse me.

312
00:21:25,984 --> 00:21:27,152
You're a coward.

313
00:21:50,676 --> 00:21:52,778
I heard you're attending
the Kyoto conference.

314
00:21:54,846 --> 00:21:58,617
I looked forward to going to
the restaurant in Nishiazabu.

315
00:21:59,284 --> 00:22:00,652
Go there with someone else.

316
00:22:02,621 --> 00:22:05,057
Maybe I should go with you to Kyoto.

317
00:22:07,025 --> 00:22:08,627
What do you want for souvenirs?

318
00:22:12,097 --> 00:22:13,198
He's a coward.

319
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:28,313
- Daimon.
- I won't do it.

320
00:22:29,715 --> 00:22:33,785
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

321
00:22:35,887 --> 00:22:39,024
Let's start this week's
preoperative conference.

322
00:22:39,858 --> 00:22:43,328
First, the patient is 37, female,
Rumiko Shijo.

323
00:22:44,096 --> 00:22:47,466
She's hospitalized
due to acute pericarditis.

324
00:22:47,933 --> 00:22:51,002
Diagnosed as pancreas cancer,
stage four.

325
00:22:51,503 --> 00:22:56,908
The tumor cell
on the distal pancreas is 5cm,

326
00:22:57,376 --> 00:22:59,644
and it invades
near the abdominal artery.

327
00:23:00,011 --> 00:23:04,149
Due to the aneurism on abdominal
aorta, the cancer can't be removed.

328
00:23:05,350 --> 00:23:06,585
I can remove it.

329
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:12,124
No way. The tumor invades
over nerves and vessels.

330
00:23:12,491 --> 00:23:17,229
I'd do distal pancreatectomy
to remove them all.

331
00:23:19,898 --> 00:23:20,766
Are you serious?

332
00:23:21,199 --> 00:23:23,201
Even if you removed the entire tumor,

333
00:23:23,702 --> 00:23:25,103
what about the aneurism?

334
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:29,541
It can be ruptured during surgery
and the patient may die.

335
00:23:29,875 --> 00:23:32,644
Is there any disadvantage
if she's saved?

336
00:23:34,546 --> 00:23:36,615
- Don't be ridiculous!
- I'm right.

337
00:23:37,382 --> 00:23:38,250
Daimon.

338
00:23:39,985 --> 00:23:44,990
Are you going to kill this patient?

339
00:23:45,390 --> 00:23:50,495
You wish for her death, don't you?

340
00:23:50,829 --> 00:23:53,031
Daimon! That's enough.

341
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:53,932
Ebina.

342
00:23:58,703 --> 00:23:59,604
Daimon,

343
00:24:01,540 --> 00:24:04,009
how can I explain...

344
00:24:06,344 --> 00:24:11,216
Your strong confidence.

345
00:24:13,652 --> 00:24:17,556
I have no idea where you got it from.

346
00:24:19,658 --> 00:24:20,492
Listen.

347
00:24:21,626 --> 00:24:25,831
Everybody makes mistakes.

348
00:24:26,398 --> 00:24:28,733
We, as doctors, are not almighty.

349
00:24:31,470 --> 00:24:38,410
I give top priority to our patients' lives
as a humble human being.

350
00:24:39,578 --> 00:24:41,847
That's what doctors should be.

351
00:24:42,581 --> 00:24:45,250
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

352
00:24:46,852 --> 00:24:47,953
You're a coward.

353
00:24:51,656 --> 00:24:53,492
- Get her out of here.
- Okay.

354
00:24:53,558 --> 00:24:54,392
Yes, sir.

355
00:24:55,093 --> 00:24:56,895
Wait.

356
00:24:59,564 --> 00:25:00,398
Open the door.

357
00:25:04,903 --> 00:25:06,338
Coward?

358
00:25:14,379 --> 00:25:17,482
Don't let Daimon close to Rumiko.

359
00:25:18,817 --> 00:25:20,719
Don't let her perform the surgery.

360
00:25:21,453 --> 00:25:22,954
It will never ever happen.

361
00:25:23,488 --> 00:25:24,322
Yes, sir.

362
00:25:26,825 --> 00:25:27,659
Prof. Hiruma,

363
00:25:28,326 --> 00:25:29,361
your car has arrived.

364
00:25:29,427 --> 00:25:30,962
- Okay.
- Excuse me.

365
00:25:37,435 --> 00:25:39,471
I am looking forward to my souvenir.

366
00:25:41,339 --> 00:25:42,707
Sure.

367
00:25:44,609 --> 00:25:45,577
Excuse me.

368
00:25:46,111 --> 00:25:47,712
Ready for job hopping?

369
00:25:53,585 --> 00:25:55,520
May I perform surgery on you?

370
00:25:57,622 --> 00:25:59,991
If I don't do that, you'll die.

371
00:26:01,359 --> 00:26:03,862
No surgeon in this hospital will do it .

372
00:26:04,195 --> 00:26:05,297
But you're a part-timer.

373
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:07,265
I'm a freelance surgeon.

374
00:26:08,066 --> 00:26:09,668
I'm running my business in Ginza.

375
00:26:10,669 --> 00:26:12,704
I believe in job titles and powers.

376
00:26:13,171 --> 00:26:16,641
I've adjusted myself to live for it.

377
00:26:17,342 --> 00:26:19,010
Surely I got screwed sometimes.

378
00:26:20,979 --> 00:26:24,616
But I can't leave my life
to a part-timer.

379
00:26:26,618 --> 00:26:30,121
You can be saved.
You're a coward.

380
00:26:31,323 --> 00:26:32,257
What did you say?

381
00:26:32,324 --> 00:26:34,392
I said you'll be absolutely saved.

382
00:26:35,994 --> 00:26:37,429
How can you say "absolutely?"

383
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:42,901
Because I never fail.

384
00:26:46,805 --> 00:26:47,639
Get out.

385
00:26:54,913 --> 00:26:57,983
I reserved Hayashi in Gion.

386
00:26:58,149 --> 00:27:01,686
Enjoy the best
tea-ceremony dish in Kyoto tonight.

387
00:27:01,953 --> 00:27:05,423
Hayashi?
That is a wonderful restaurant.

388
00:27:06,324 --> 00:27:07,325
Have a safe trip.

389
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:12,731
Pay extra attention while I'm away.

390
00:27:14,332 --> 00:27:16,635
- Understood?
- Yes, sir.

391
00:27:16,701 --> 00:27:17,535
See you.

392
00:27:19,904 --> 00:27:22,474
- I thought Dr. Ebina would go.
- Don't mention it.

393
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:29,814
Here.

394
00:27:31,116 --> 00:27:32,751
Thanks.

395
00:27:37,956 --> 00:27:39,424
- We're off.
- Okay.

396
00:27:47,265 --> 00:27:48,600
Have a safe trip.

397
00:27:54,272 --> 00:27:55,507
We don't have much time...

398
00:28:15,794 --> 00:28:19,664
Are you sure you can do
distal pancreatectomy?

399
00:28:21,299 --> 00:28:25,437
Including surrounding areas,
all tumor cells can be removed.

400
00:28:25,503 --> 00:28:27,706
What about the Quality of Life?

401
00:28:28,006 --> 00:28:32,510
Since healthy organs remain,
the QOL will be improved.

402
00:28:33,812 --> 00:28:35,847
The target is close to the aortic aneurysm

403
00:28:36,081 --> 00:28:38,917
as well as pancreas cancer.

404
00:28:39,584 --> 00:28:41,986
It's likely to get ruptured.

405
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:46,024
An endovascular stent graft
can prevent that risk.

406
00:28:49,627 --> 00:28:50,495
I see.

407
00:28:50,628 --> 00:28:52,964
But don't do this.

408
00:28:53,932 --> 00:28:56,101
- Why?
- Only I can do it.

409
00:29:05,744 --> 00:29:06,678
I'm sorry.

410
00:29:27,966 --> 00:29:30,335
It must be hard for Prof. Ebina.

411
00:29:31,469 --> 00:29:33,404
How can you say that?

412
00:29:35,006 --> 00:29:37,375
You and I got surpassed by that outsider

413
00:29:38,076 --> 00:29:40,812
who graduated
from some regional college.

414
00:29:42,347 --> 00:29:45,083
The university hospital is
like a private corporation, huh?

415
00:29:47,252 --> 00:29:49,754
Good for you, freelancer.

416
00:29:49,921 --> 00:29:52,290
You'll never get surpassed.

417
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:54,392
What?

418
00:29:54,626 --> 00:29:55,860
Do you have a problem?

419
00:29:58,530 --> 00:30:00,098
It's time to go home.

420
00:30:00,865 --> 00:30:03,568
Shijo is in emergency.

421
00:30:21,486 --> 00:30:22,487
Do you feel pain here?

422
00:30:35,466 --> 00:30:38,236
We've got to
do an emergency operation.

423
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:40,805
- No.
- We need Ebina's permission.

424
00:30:40,872 --> 00:30:44,008
- I can't find him.
- What?

425
00:30:44,209 --> 00:30:45,910
- Hurry.
- Yes, ma'am.

426
00:30:49,480 --> 00:30:50,448
Can't catch him?

427
00:30:50,815 --> 00:30:52,016
Only voice message.

428
00:30:52,650 --> 00:30:56,187
Where did he go in this situation?

429
00:31:06,965 --> 00:31:09,767
EXECUTIVE MANAGER
OF SURGERY DEPARTMENT

430
00:31:16,174 --> 00:31:18,476
I can't get a hold of any doctors.

431
00:31:19,143 --> 00:31:21,379
Insert a stent graft
into aortic aneurysm.

432
00:31:21,579 --> 00:31:24,449
- Let's wait for the permission.
- If you feel uneasy, get out.

433
00:31:26,384 --> 00:31:27,685
- I understand.
- Scalpel.

434
00:31:34,425 --> 00:31:36,961
Insert the sheath into both groins.
Guide wire.

435
00:32:01,552 --> 00:32:05,623
EXECUTIVE MANAGER
OF SURGERY DEPARTMENT

436
00:32:16,434 --> 00:32:18,870
Reached the aortic aneurysm.
Place the stent graft.

437
00:32:26,377 --> 00:32:29,314
Place the supportive stent
on the opposite side.

438
00:32:29,414 --> 00:32:30,381
Yes, ma'am.

439
00:32:31,482 --> 00:32:32,383
Excuse me.

440
00:32:36,054 --> 00:32:38,589
The vessels are thin. Be careful.

441
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:51,202
Blood pressure is dropping.

442
00:32:51,536 --> 00:32:55,239
The upper is 39,
and the lower cannot be measured.

443
00:33:05,483 --> 00:33:06,951
KYOTO

444
00:33:13,491 --> 00:33:14,959
Matsutake mushrooms smell great.

445
00:33:16,894 --> 00:33:17,829
Are you okay?

446
00:33:18,763 --> 00:33:19,597
Your phone.

447
00:33:21,366 --> 00:33:23,434
I don't know this number.

448
00:33:26,871 --> 00:33:28,206
He hung up.

449
00:33:28,806 --> 00:33:29,974
This is no good.

450
00:33:30,508 --> 00:33:32,977
Let's say, we are not here.

451
00:33:33,578 --> 00:33:34,479
Yes, sir.

452
00:33:34,545 --> 00:33:36,214
The iliac artery is damaged.

453
00:33:36,414 --> 00:33:38,416
Bring a balloon catheter. Move!

454
00:33:40,852 --> 00:33:42,920
Hold the guide wire.

455
00:33:43,154 --> 00:33:44,155
Yes, ma'am.

456
00:33:58,102 --> 00:33:58,936
Dr. Ebina.

457
00:33:59,203 --> 00:34:00,638
I take care of the stent graft.

458
00:34:05,977 --> 00:34:08,579
- Move stent graft to the damaged area.
- Yes, sir.

459
00:34:11,949 --> 00:34:14,152
I expand the balloon
and stop the bleeding.

460
00:34:23,928 --> 00:34:26,998
- It stopped bleeding.
- The blood pressure is 80/50.

461
00:34:27,265 --> 00:34:30,601
Roger. Then deploy the stent graft.

462
00:34:30,935 --> 00:34:33,271
I deploy the stent graft.

463
00:34:51,222 --> 00:34:53,524
I detach the pancreatic body.

464
00:35:25,189 --> 00:35:26,257
Good job, guys.

465
00:35:32,263 --> 00:35:33,131
What?

466
00:35:34,765 --> 00:35:35,600
The surgery?

467
00:35:37,368 --> 00:35:41,305
Yes. We removed all the tumor cells.

468
00:35:42,140 --> 00:35:42,974
Ebina,

469
00:35:44,375 --> 00:35:45,543
did you perform it?

470
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:47,478
No, Daimon did it.

471
00:35:48,179 --> 00:35:51,949
I told you not to
let her perform surgery!

472
00:35:53,117 --> 00:35:54,352
What were you doing?

473
00:35:55,953 --> 00:35:56,787
Ebina,

474
00:35:58,122 --> 00:35:59,390
be prepared.

475
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:11,035
That's like Dr. Daimon.

476
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:13,704
Damn you, Ebina.

477
00:36:14,906 --> 00:36:16,974
I've taken care of you...

478
00:36:18,276 --> 00:36:20,545
That big dog went against me.

479
00:36:24,649 --> 00:36:27,451
This little puppy is adorable though.

480
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:51,576
Those professors said they can't
perform surgery, but you did.

481
00:36:53,110 --> 00:36:55,513
I told you I never fail.

482
00:36:57,148 --> 00:37:00,985
The surgery was a success
not because of you.

483
00:37:02,286 --> 00:37:05,556
That's because of my luck.

484
00:37:07,024 --> 00:37:08,092
Are you serious?

485
00:37:15,066 --> 00:37:15,900
Here.

486
00:37:18,369 --> 00:37:19,237
Keep it.

487
00:37:21,005 --> 00:37:21,839
What's this?

488
00:37:22,773 --> 00:37:27,912
Everyone wants to
have power someday,

489
00:37:29,146 --> 00:37:30,915
even if you don't care about it now.

490
00:37:32,783 --> 00:37:37,822
I'm looking forward to seeing
how you use that note pad.

491
00:37:45,596 --> 00:37:50,201
Will I live until then?

492
00:37:55,773 --> 00:37:56,674
I'll take it then.

493
00:37:57,775 --> 00:37:59,644
Visit my bar anytime.

494
00:38:00,978 --> 00:38:02,647
I'll hire you with extra pay.

495
00:38:15,326 --> 00:38:16,260
Thank you...

496
00:38:28,606 --> 00:38:29,774
She's already woken up.

497
00:38:33,611 --> 00:38:34,478
Excuse me.

498
00:38:39,850 --> 00:38:42,553
I've worked more than 12 hours
overtime.

499
00:38:42,620 --> 00:38:44,388
I'm starving.

500
00:38:47,892 --> 00:38:50,661
- Daimon.
- Yes?

501
00:38:51,262 --> 00:38:52,797
- Where is the note pad?
- The note pad?

502
00:38:52,863 --> 00:38:55,499
- Rumiko's note pad.
- Oh. I threw it away.

503
00:38:56,801 --> 00:38:59,337
You threw it away? Where?

504
00:38:59,570 --> 00:39:01,105
- In a trash can.
- Which one?

505
00:39:01,238 --> 00:39:02,273
You scare me.

506
00:39:02,406 --> 00:39:06,377
It's not here.

507
00:39:07,545 --> 00:39:10,748
Not here.

508
00:39:13,284 --> 00:39:17,955
Wait up! Wait! Sorry.

509
00:39:20,691 --> 00:39:22,393
Where is it? Excuse me.

510
00:39:31,369 --> 00:39:35,039
Here it is! Oh my!

511
00:39:37,742 --> 00:39:39,577
Thanks.

512
00:39:41,746 --> 00:39:43,280
I was right.

513
00:39:44,315 --> 00:39:46,717
- What?
- I knew something went on with you.

514
00:39:46,784 --> 00:39:51,422
Her pulse was not abnormal enough to
beep the electrocardiogram.

515
00:39:55,826 --> 00:39:58,129
You made it beep on purpose, right?

516
00:40:00,431 --> 00:40:03,000
- Why would...
- So that I would perform the surgery

517
00:40:03,134 --> 00:40:04,402
because you can't do that.

518
00:40:05,703 --> 00:40:09,707
If all went well, she promised
you could have that note pad.

519
00:40:11,609 --> 00:40:13,177
It's too simple.

520
00:40:15,579 --> 00:40:17,715
What a nasty idea you could think of.

521
00:40:18,849 --> 00:40:19,683
It's unbelievable.

522
00:40:19,750 --> 00:40:21,452
- Then return it to me.
- No way.

523
00:40:21,952 --> 00:40:24,388
I found this note pad.
This is not yours.

524
00:40:25,623 --> 00:40:28,125
It's too simple.

525
00:40:46,977 --> 00:40:47,978
Welcome back.

526
00:40:48,112 --> 00:40:49,413
Welcome back.

527
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:51,182
What is my souvenir?

528
00:40:51,315 --> 00:40:53,150
Usawa. Call Ebina.

529
00:40:53,317 --> 00:40:54,418
Yes, sir.

530
00:40:57,521 --> 00:40:58,422
Now!

531
00:41:00,024 --> 00:41:01,192
Yatsuhashi sweet beans.

532
00:41:13,137 --> 00:41:14,071
This is such a mess!

533
00:41:14,505 --> 00:41:15,372
What is it?

534
00:41:15,473 --> 00:41:17,641
Prof. Ebina is going to be sent away.

535
00:41:17,741 --> 00:41:20,077
- Really?
- Everybody's talking about it.

536
00:41:20,244 --> 00:41:21,479
Will I have to join him?

537
00:41:21,912 --> 00:41:23,247
I was his assistant.

538
00:41:23,881 --> 00:41:24,982
You'll be fine.

539
00:41:25,115 --> 00:41:27,651
This doctor is in big trouble.

540
00:41:27,718 --> 00:41:30,788
- But she is a part-timer.
- I'm a freelancer.

541
00:41:31,155 --> 00:41:34,492
Dr. Daimon?

542
00:41:34,558 --> 00:41:35,392
What?

543
00:41:35,559 --> 00:41:39,530
Please come to
Executive Manager Hiruma's office.

544
00:41:39,597 --> 00:41:40,431
What for?

545
00:41:40,865 --> 00:41:43,234
EXECUTIVE MANAGER
OF SURGERY DEPARTMENT

546
00:41:43,300 --> 00:41:44,435
Why did you do the surgery?

547
00:41:44,568 --> 00:41:45,803
She'd have died.

548
00:41:45,870 --> 00:41:47,671
That's not my question.

549
00:41:50,174 --> 00:41:51,041
Let me explain.

550
00:41:57,815 --> 00:41:59,149
This is all about this note pad.

551
00:42:10,227 --> 00:42:12,296
Ebina.

552
00:42:14,098 --> 00:42:17,268
Are you threatening me?

553
00:42:24,008 --> 00:42:29,813
You remember who gave you
the current position.

554
00:42:29,914 --> 00:42:30,781
Right, Ebina?

555
00:42:33,918 --> 00:42:35,886
This is how you choose to repay me?

556
00:42:39,690 --> 00:42:41,659
Are you betraying me?

557
00:42:42,626 --> 00:42:44,061
You son of a bitch!

558
00:42:47,398 --> 00:42:48,566
Answer me, Ebina.

559
00:42:56,574 --> 00:42:58,042
You...

560
00:43:09,219 --> 00:43:13,424
Our enemy is not in Honno-ji Temple.

561
00:43:14,358 --> 00:43:15,459
Huh?

562
00:43:42,052 --> 00:43:42,886
You ate them.

563
00:43:49,059 --> 00:43:50,127
Ebina...

564
00:43:51,895 --> 00:43:54,231
Oh my goodness.

565
00:43:56,133 --> 00:43:58,435
How great you are...

566
00:44:22,092 --> 00:44:23,560
I'm honored.

567
00:44:25,062 --> 00:44:27,197
You're such a great man.

568
00:44:33,070 --> 00:44:35,305
What the heck is going on?

569
00:44:36,507 --> 00:44:39,543
- I'm obliged.
- Here you go...

570
00:44:48,986 --> 00:44:51,288
You helped someone's promotion.

571
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:53,023
Surgery is my hobby.

572
00:44:53,490 --> 00:44:56,093
Why don't you stand on my side?

573
00:44:57,461 --> 00:44:58,962
I won't.

574
00:45:09,840 --> 00:45:12,142
Here's a melon and the bill.

575
00:45:18,115 --> 00:45:19,149
What?

576
00:45:20,050 --> 00:45:21,985
How is it so expensive?

577
00:45:30,594 --> 00:45:33,530
That includes the price of this note pad.

578
00:45:35,332 --> 00:45:39,803
I apologize to
charge for the price of your life.

579
00:45:40,437 --> 00:45:44,508
Daimon and I will take this secret

580
00:45:45,142 --> 00:45:47,478
to our graves with us.

581
00:45:49,179 --> 00:45:52,549
If the price of your life deserves
better, I will reconsider it.

582
00:45:53,550 --> 00:45:57,988
Well...This is fine.

583
00:46:00,290 --> 00:46:01,125
Thank you. Here.

584
00:46:02,259 --> 00:46:03,093
Thanks.

585
00:46:05,329 --> 00:46:06,563
Was this pad there?

586
00:46:17,274 --> 00:46:21,111
<i>This woman hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

587
00:46:22,112 --> 00:46:25,282
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and her on-the-job experience</i>

588
00:46:25,783 --> 00:46:27,117
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

589
00:46:27,284 --> 00:46:28,285
Michiko!

590
00:46:28,352 --> 00:46:31,188
Why did you
throw away that note pad?

591
00:46:31,789 --> 00:46:35,859
If we had it,
we could've gotten more money.

592
00:46:36,627 --> 00:46:40,998
You've got to work harder
and repay your debt.

593
00:46:42,065 --> 00:46:44,067
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

594
00:46:44,601 --> 00:46:47,304
<i>also known as Doctor X.</i>

595
00:46:49,006 --> 00:46:50,908
He has Buddha's hands.

596
00:46:50,974 --> 00:46:52,376
It sounds so dubious.

597
00:46:52,509 --> 00:46:55,679
There is a trick to succeed 100%
in his operations.

598
00:46:55,813 --> 00:46:58,448
He's evil, as opposed to God.

599
00:46:58,515 --> 00:47:01,585
The mission is complete.
I never fail.

600
00:47:01,652 --> 00:47:03,821
I never fail.
